# Sale Deed AI - line-ending policy.
#
# Git normally converts line endings on checkout. For source that is harmless.
# For the extraction prompt it is not: the model was fine-tuned against that
# exact text, and a checkout on another machine that turned its 19 bare LFs
# into CRLFs would hand the model a different prompt to the one it was trained
# on - silently, and only on the second machine.
#
# Matched by basename because the folder it lives in has a space in it, which
# .gitattributes has no reliable way to escape. The name is unique in the tree.
prompt_v6_short.txt -text

# Batch files are read by cmd.exe, which needs CRLF. Checked out with CRLF on
# every platform, so a clone made on Linux still produces a runnable installer.
*.bat text eol=crlf
